  "title": "23rd European Medtech & Healthcare Services Conference \u2014 Key Takeaways",
  "type": "sector",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-09-12",
  "insights": [
   "The conference highlighted innovation as a primary driver for growth and market share gains across the European Medtech sector.",
   "China remains a strategically essential market despite ongoing headwinds from volume-based procurement (VBP) and increased local competition.",
   "Rising cost inflation is a common theme, with companies accelerating productivity programs and leveraging global manufacturing footprints to protect margins.",
   "Ambu faces temporary volume issues in US Anesthesia & Patient Monitoring, but remains confident in its long-term single-use conversion thesis.",
   "Carl Zeiss Meditec is focused on its 'ProfitUp' margin-recovery program, targeting \u20ac200m gross contribution by 2028-29.",
   "Convatec is at an inflection point with growth accelerating across chronic-care categories, supported by a strong innovation pipeline.",
   "Demant is seeing recovery in Hearing Care and Diagnostics, with KIND integration running ahead of expectations.",
   "Fresenius Medical Care is addressing US SMTG softness through improved referral capture and patient intake measures.",
   "IBA sees substantial potential for Proton Therapy adoption as clinical evidence and reimbursement economics evolve.",
   "Philips is accelerating structural cost savings to offset margin pressure from higher cost inflation following the war in Iran.",
   "Roche expects Diagnostics growth to accelerate toward the top end of its mid-to-high single-digit guidance after 2027/28 as China headwinds ease.",
   "Smith & Nephew is looking to the LANDMARK launch to fill a portfolio gap in US knees and support a recovery in H2 2026.",
   "Sonova continues to gain market share, supported by the Phonak EON platform and strong commercial execution.",
   "Straumann is leveraging its Shanghai campus for both China market competitiveness and COGS efficiency for other Asian markets.",
   "Tecan remains cautious on the near-term market outlook but is confident in its 'Rewired' transformation program to meet 2028 targets."
  ],
